## SQ-DM-03 | dandelion maturing: fertile soil about twice as fast as rich soil
@group A
@commands Dandelions on Rich Soil and Fertile Soil, `/gamerule randomTickSpeed 300`
@pass Fertile Soil matures about twice as fast as Rich Soil (`fertileSoilTicks = 10`, `richSoilTicks = 20`)
@fails the config file still holds the old values
@reviewed 2026-11-17
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> fill 20 -61 30 29 -61 30 farmersdelight:rich_soil
> fill 20 -61 32 29 -61 32 immersive_weathering:mulch_block
> fill 20 -60 30 29 -60 30 minecraft:dandelion
> fill 20 -60 32 29 -60 32 minecraft:dandelion
> cdevtest randomtick 20 -61 30 29 -60 32 5
> cdevtest count 20 -60 30 29 -60 30 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
> cdevtest count 20 -60 32 29 -60 32 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
> cdevtest randomtick 20 -61 30 29 -60 32 5
> cdevtest count 20 -60 30 29 -60 30 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
> cdevtest count 20 -60 32 29 -60 32 veggiesdelight:mature_dandelion
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look count lines alternate rich (z 30), fertile (z 32): fertile matures about twice as fast as rich at each read (5 random ticks per block per round = the old 30 s at randomTickSpeed 30); fertile soil id may differ (record the fill error if any)
